            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Abrasive clogs immediately on an uncured film and you embed debris into the soft material, making removal harder. Diagnose the cause first: if it is mix ratio, remove it; if it is cold or moisture, warmth and time may still resolve it without any mechanical intervention."
