        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Diagnose before you wait, because this is the one sealing problem where patience is sometimes the wrong response. Uniform tackiness on a two-part product means the mix ratio or the mixing, and that never cures no matter how long you leave it — the material has to come off. Patchy sticky spots mean unmixed resin from the container walls or contamination.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tackiness with cloudiness and blistering points at moisture still coming out of a slab that was sealed too soon, and cold points at a slab that never reached reaction temperature. Both of those often recover with warmth, ventilation and one to three weeks. Whatever the cause, do not coat over it, do not sand it and do not wash it — all three turn a recoverable problem into a removal job.
          </p>
        </div>

